\title{Logical equivalence}
\date{2026-01-28T21:17:59Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Definition}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Two propositions that always have the same truth value are \em{logically equivalent}, written #{P \equiv Q}.  Alternatively, #{P \equiv Q} when #{P \iff Q} is a [tautology](0041).}
